h("ABSTRACT"); par("RideShare is a web-based vehicle rental and sharing management system that connects vehicle owners and renters through a centralized digital platform. The system is intended to simplify vehicle discovery, listing management, availability verification, booking coordination, location handling, payment processing, and post-rental records. It is designed as a role-aware application in which authenticated organization members may act as vehicle owners, renters, or both depending on the workflow, while administrators manage verification and moderation activities.")
par("The implementation uses a React and Vite client, an Express REST API, and MongoDB accessed through Mongoose. The inspected source includes vehicle catalogue and nearby search, owner-managed listings, date-range availability checks, quotations, booking lifecycle management, notifications, reviews, invoices, route previews, protected tracking endpoints, pricing suggestions, and a natural-language recommendation interface. Clerk is used for authentication and organization membership, ImageKit for media uploads, and Razorpay for payment operations when payment configuration is enabled. Location services can use Google Maps and fall back to Nominatim and OSRM where appropriate.")
par("The report presents the theoretical background, literature survey, requirements, feasibility, system architecture, data model, algorithms, implementation approach, testing strategy, results, limitations, and future scope. The report distinguishes implemented source modules from features that require valid credentials, external service availability, browser permission, or production deployment. The future scope emphasizes automated testing, security hardening, privacy-aware tracking, payment reconciliation, richer recommendations, mobile access, analytics, and operational support.")
